# text = The Marchioness retired as Vivian assured her And as she retired , she murmured her gratitude gracefully to Julie's young physician said his Lordship , endeavouring to recover his dignity Vivian had not much difficulty in collecting his ideas , and he proceeded , not as displeased as his Lordship with the domestic scene The Marquess breathed aloud said the agitated Peer said the Peer , in a low voice ; and then his Lordship looked anxiously round the room , as if he feared that there had been some mysterious witness to his whisper said Vivian , and he drew his chair close to the Marquess said Vivian , whispering most earnestly in the Marquess's ear , and laying his hand upon his Lordship's arm The Marquess's eyes smiled with triumph , as he shook Vivian cordially by the hand , and begged him to call upon him on the morrow
