# text = The subdued satire of his keen eye burst out for an instant , and he looked as if he would have said Vivian had , unbidden , seated himself by the side of Mr . Cleveland's library table ; and , not knowing exactly how to proceed , was employing himself by making a calculation whether there were more black than white spots on the body of the old Newfoundland , who was now apparently happily slumbering continued the Newfoundland's master Now this was precisely the thing which Vivian had determined not to do ; and so he diplomatised , in order to gain time said that gentleman , with a somewhat disappointed air said Vivian , with one of his sweetest cadences and looking up to Mr . Cleveland's face with an eye expressive of all kindness again exclaimed Cleveland , looking very anxious , and moving restlessly on his library chair interrupted Mr . Cleveland , who began to suspect that the envoy was no greenhorn
