# text = Vivian made one or two ineffectual struggles to bring the Marquess to a business-like habit of mind , but his Lordship never dared to trust himself alone with Cleveland , and , indeed , almost lost the power of speech when in presence of the future leader of his party ; so , in the morning , the Marquess played off the two Lords and Sir Berdmore against his former friend , and then , to compensate for not meeting Mr . Cleveland in the morning , he was particularly courteous to him at dinner-time , and asked him always and invariably took wine with him .
