# text = When the novelty has worn off , when we have discovered that the new characters differ little from all others we have met before , and that the scene they inhabit is only another variety of the great order we have so often observed , we relapse into our ancient habits of inattention ; we think more of ourselves , and less of those we meet ; and musing our moments away in reverie , or in a vain attempt to cheat the coming day of the monotony of the present one , we begin to find that the various-vested hours have bounded and are bounding away in a course at once imperceptible , uninteresting , and unprofitable .
