# text = The drawings were vivid representations of the scenery which they professed to depict , and Vivian forgot his melancholy as he attracted the attention of the fair artist to points of interest unknown or unnoticed by the guide-books and the diaries said Lady Madeleine to Vivian said Miss Fane said Vivian said Violet said Miss Fane observed Vivian said Miss Fane said Vivian said Miss Fane muttered Vivian for he thought of one whom he had sent to his great account before his time said Lady Madeleine But Miss Fane would not leave the subject said her Ladyship Miss Fane rose and sat down to the instrument .
