# text = The Prince and Vivian amused themselves by endeavouring to form some conception of the person , manners , and habits of the remarkable man to whom they were on the point of paying so interesting a visit said Vivian After a ride of five hours , the horsemen arrived at a small village said the Prince While they were hesitating as to whom they should address , an equestrian , who had already passed them on the road , though at some distance , came up , and inquired , in a voice which Vivian recognised as that of the messenger who had brought Beckendorff's letter to Turriparva , whether he had the honour of addressing Mr . von Philipson .
