# text = Two days after the receipt of this letter Essper George ran into the room with a much less solemn physiognomy than he had thought proper to assume since his master's arrival at Reisenburg asked Vivian , with eagerness , for , as is always the case when such questions are asked us , he was thinking of every person in the world except the right one continued Essper thought Vivian said Essper said Vivian said Essper , with a look of great disappointment said his master continued Essper About a week after his arrival at Reisenburg , as Vivian was at breakfast , the door opened , and Mr . Sievers entered said Mr . Sievers , smiling said Vivian , as he greeted him cordially said Mr . Sievers said Sievers said Vivian said Sievers said Sievers , bowing The gentlemen accordingly left the hotel ; and proceeding down the principal street of the New Town , they came into a large square , or Place d'Armes .
