# text = The Archduchess had not yet seen the Crown Prince ; but six miniatures and a whole length portrait had prepared her for not meeting an Adonis or a Baron Trenck , and that was all ; for never had the Correggio of the age of Charles the Fifth better substantiated his claims to the office of Court painter than by these accurate semblances of his Royal Highness , in which his hump was subdued into a Grecian bend , and his lack-lustre eyes seemed beaming with tenderness and admiration .
